#[navbar]

#[section, $md:
    @../../ (Documentation) / @../ (Packages and imports) / Core packages

    # Core packages

    Core packages form small, typed packages owned by the compiler and selected
    for availability by a builder. They do not act as ordinary source files in
    your project, but they import with the same `import` syntax.

    Most Core packages require explicit imports. The prelude keeps only the
    smallest always-available surface bare, such as `io`.

    Builder support can vary. The @../../progress (progress matrix) owns the
    source of truth for current package and backend support. The HTML builder
    currently supports optional core packages on the JavaScript path.

    ## Package pages

    - @prelude (Prelude policy)
    - @io (Core IO)
    - @collections (Core collections)
    - @math (Core math)
    - @text (Core text)
    - @random (Core random)
    - @time (Core time)
]

